# Branch & release policy

- Keep **one** long-lived branch: `main`. Do not use `master`, `dev`, or parallel permanent branches.
- **Build and Release** runs on push to `main` (or manual `workflow_dispatch`).
- Day-to-day work and releases both happen on `main`. Bump `package.json` version when you want a packaged GitHub Release, then push `main`.
- Do not rely on `git tag` / `git push origin v*` to start the release workflow.
- Short-lived feature branches are optional; merge/delete them promptly after landing on `main`.
